  "description": "CUR-POP (F: why the ORDER BY snapshot of the first card reported 2048 at open), variant: a snapshot over SELECT ... ORDER BY ID on the 8-row table Sm. Part 1: RecordCount at open, after a field read, after MoveNext and MoveLast. Part 2 (a new snapshot): read ID and V of row 1, then another call runs UPDATE Sm SET V = 'chg' WHERE ID IN (2, 4, 8) (dbFailOnError); MoveFirst and ID and V are read, then Move 1, 2, 4 (cumulative) reading ID and V each time. Decides whether the count at open and the fixing of values follow ORDER BY or table size.",
